{{also|Stiff}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|stiff}}, {{m|enm|stiffe}}, {{m|enm|stif}}, from {{inh|en|ang|stīf}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*stīf}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*stīfaz}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*steypós}}.

See also {{cog|fy|stiif}}, {{cog|nl|stijf}}, {{cog|nb|stiv}}, {{cog|de|steif}}; also {{cog|la|stīpes}}, {{m|la|stīpō}}, from which English {{m|en|stevedore}}.

The expected Modern English form would be {{IPAchar|/staɪf/}}; {{IPAchar|/stɪf/}} is probably originally from compounds such as {{m|en|stiffly}}, where the vowel was shortened before a consonant cluster.<ref>{{R:Jespersen MEGoHP|I|4.35|124}}</ref>

