===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|slang|chiefly|North America}} An average person, usually male, of no particular distinction, skill, or education.
#: {{ux|en|[[working stiff|working '''stiff''']]}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1943|author=w:Ayn Rand|title=w:The Fountainhead|chapter=IX|passage=The clerk shrugged: “That's the boss's little girl.” “Why, the lucky '''stiff'''!” said Keating. “He's been holding out on me.” “You misunderstood me,” the clerk said coldly. “It's his daughter. It's Dominique Francon.”}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A person who is deceived, as a [[mark]] or [[pigeon]] in a [[swindle]].
#: {{ux|en|She convinced the '''stiff''' to go to her hotel room, where her henchman was waiting to rob him.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[cadaver]]; a dead person.
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:corpse|Thesaurus:body}}
#* {{quote-av|en|title=w:Monty Python's Flying Circus|episode=Full Frontal Nudity, [[w:Dead Parrot sketch|Dead Parrot sketch]]|author=w:Monty Python|date=1969-12-07|role=w:Mr Praline|actor=w:John Cleese|passage=This parrot is no more! It has ceased to be! It's expired and gone to meet its maker! This is a late parrot! It's a '''stiff'''! Bereft of life, it rests in peace! If you hadn't nailed it to the perch it would be pushing up the daisies!}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[flop]]; a commercial failure.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1994|author=Andy Dougan|title=The actors' director: Richard Attenborough behind the camera|page=63
|passage=If the movie was a '''stiff''' it wasn't any of their specific faults. They were all in it together and they were jobbed in and jobbed out for two weeks and gone and they got a pile of money for their efforts.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2016|author=Ralph J. Gleason; Toby Gleason|title=Music in the Air: The Selected Writings of Ralph J. Gleason
|passage=They never did sell any records. I don't mean they didn't sell 100,000. I mean they didn't sell 5000. Total. National. Coast-to-coast. The record was a '''stiff'''.}}
# {{lb|en|US|slang}} A person who leaves (especially a restaurant) without paying the bill.
# {{lb|en|US|slang|by extension}} A [[customer]] who does not leave a [[tip]].
# {{lb|en|blackjack}} Any [[hard hand]] where it is possible to exceed 21 by drawing an additional card.
# {{lb|en|finance|slang}} [[negotiable instrument|Negotiable instruments]], possibly [[forge]]d.
# {{lb|en|prison slang}} A [[note]] or [[letter]] [[surreptitious]]ly sent by an inmate.

